message.content:
This is a functional unit under Section XVI Note 4 (and GRI 1), classified by the machine that performs the principal function, which is mixing. Heading 8474 covers machinery for mixing or kneading mineral substances, but the materials here (sealants, adhesives, and coatings) are chemical products. The better fit is heading 8479, specifically 8479.82 for mixing, kneading, crushing, grinding, screening, sifting, homogenizing, emulsifying or stirring machines.

I recall CBP rulings on similar planetary or butterfly mixers for sealants and adhesives that went to 8479.82.00. The HTSUS subheading is 8479.82.00 with statistical suffixes. The 8479.82 subheading breaks down as 8479.82.00 with 10-digit codes 8479.82.0010 (ultrasonic) and 8479.82.0090 (other); I believe 8479.82.0090 is "Other". The 2022 HTS has 8479.82.00 with 8479.82.0010 for ultrasonic machines and 8479.82.0090 for the rest, so I use 8479.82.0090.

{"hts_code": "8479.82.0090", "reason": "The interconnected mixing system is a functional unit (Section XVI Note 4) whose principal function is mixing, stirring and homogenizing chemical materials, so it falls under heading 8479 as a mixing/stirring machine in subheading 8479.82, in the 'other' statistical suffix."}
